<Window x:Class="ORS_ER.windows.HelpWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
        xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
        xmlns:local="clr-namespace:ORS_ER.windows"
        mc:Ignorable="d"
        Title="Help" Height="600" Width="900" Background="#F4F6F9">
    <Grid Margin="24">
        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="1*"/>
        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
        <Border Background="White" CornerRadius="8" BorderBrush="#E1E6EB" BorderThickness="1" Padding="20">
            <RichTextBox x:Name="Help" IsReadOnly="True" BorderThickness="0" Background="Transparent" FontSize="16" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
                <FlowDocument FontFamily="Segoe UI" PagePadding="0" TextAlignment="Left">
                    <Paragraph FontSize="32" TextAlignment="Center" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,12">
                        How to use this simulator
                    </Paragraph>

                    <Paragraph FontSize="20" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,12,0,6">1. What is this?</Paragraph>
                    <Paragraph Margin="0,0,0,8">
                        This is a Flowchart and Logic Gate simulator in one application. Use the selection box in the top-left corner
                        to switch between simulations and see the currently active mode.
                    </Paragraph>

                    <Paragraph FontSize="20" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,12,0,6">2. Menu bar</Paragraph>
                    <Paragraph Margin="0,0,0,8">
                        Here you can work with your designed flowchart or circuit.
                        In
                        <Bold>File</Bold> you have options to create new diagram by clicking on
                        <Bold>New</Bold>. Use
                        <Bold>Save As</Bold> to store your work as a
                        <Bold>JSON</Bold> file, or use
                        <Bold>Save</Bold> to save your current design to already loaded file.
                        <Bold>Load</Bold> is used to open your work in simulator. In Logic Gate simulation, you can store
                        the current circuit as a reusable component with
                        <Bold>Save component</Bold> and load custom components with
                        <Bold>Load component</Bold> . You can also export the current diagram with
                        <Bold>Export PNG</Bold> to save an image of the diagram.
                        You can also see keybinds used for different commands in their names.
                        <LineBreak/>
                        <LineBreak/>
                        In
                        <Bold>Edit</Bold> you can
                        <Bold>Copy, Paste, Duplicate and Delete</Bold> your elements as well as
                        <Bold>Undo</Bold> and
                        <Bold>Redo</Bold> your changes.
                    </Paragraph>

                    <Paragraph FontSize="20" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,12,0,6">3. Simulation</Paragraph>
                    <Paragraph Margin="0,0,0,8">
                        The simulation runs automatically every time you add or remove blocks or connections, or when you modify block
                        values. To run it manually, click
                        <Bold>Run</Bold> in the menu bar.
                    </Paragraph>
                    <Paragraph Margin="0,0,0,8">
                        Add elements to the canvas by selecting them from the list on the left, then clicking on the canvas where you
                        want them placed.
                    </Paragraph>
                    <Paragraph Margin="0,0,0,8">
                        Select elements on the canvas by clicking them; the outline turns red. Drag with the
                        <Bold>left mouse button</Bold> to reposition. Press
                        <Bold>Delete</Bold> to remove the selected element.
                    </Paragraph>
                    <Paragraph Margin="0,0,0,8">
                        In Flowchart simulation,
                        <Bold>right click</Bold> the center of an element to set values, create comparisons, perform operations,
                        or modify variables. In Logic Gate simulation,
                        <Bold>right click</Bold> an input to toggle its value between true and false.
                    </Paragraph>
                    <Paragraph Margin="0,0,0,0">
                        Create connections by clicking the
                        <Bold>black</Bold> output circle on a block. A line will follow your cursor.
                        Click the
                        <Bold>grey</Bold> input circle on another block to complete the connection. Cancel with the
                        <Bold>right mouse button</Bold> . Select a connection to highlight it, then press
                        <Bold>Delete</Bold> to remove it.
                    </Paragraph>
                </FlowDocument>
            </RichTextBox>
        </Border>
    </Grid>
</Window>
